# Findings accepted as unfixable, with reasons. Trivy reads this file
# automatically when scans run from the repo root (as CI does).
#
# The three entries below are pip's *vendored* copies of msgpack and
# setuptools/pkg_resources (site-packages/pip/_vendor/vendor.txt), not
# installed packages — `pip install -U ...` cannot touch them, and as of
# pip 26.2.1 no released pip bumps them (setuptools==70.3.0 persists even
# on pip main). The vulnerable code paths (easy_install/PackageIndex,
# msgpack deserialization of untrusted input) are not reachable through
# pip's internal use. The Dockerfile self-upgrades pip on every build, so
# these clear automatically once a pip release bumps the pins —
# re-evaluate when that happens.

# setuptools (vendored in pip): path traversal in PackageIndex.download
CVE-2025-47273
# setuptools (vendored in pip)
CVE-2026-59890
# msgpack (vendored in pip): pip main already bumps to 1.2.1, unreleased
